sted to his instagram  stating that he would be playing the  character that was quickly changed to  just say that he is in the film  however david harbour himself who of  course is going to be playing red  guardian in the film  kind of spoiled everything a few weeks  ago in his instagram post a few weeks  ago he said  ursa elena nat cd  sputnik i and all the rest of the winter  guard  look forward to sharing a popcorn bag  and a big old screen in a dark theater  with you on july 9th  the first word he said was ursa which is  ursa major the mutant the person who has  the ability to turn into a giant  bear and of course the other characters  he mentioned are the rest of the winter  guard but let's keep this focused on the  mutants for now  bottom line is he confirmed a mutant  ursa major will indeed be in black widow  so mutants are going to start to be  introduced in the mcu  less than a month from now which is  insanely exciting because obviously with  the fantastic four coming  the actual x-men team will eventually be  coming as well  and that setup is going to begin in  phase 4. i also want to add the  possibility of doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness introducing  mutants it is not confirmed to be  introducing any but it is literally  a movie that can do whatever it wants in  a movie that involves the multiverse  there are really no limits  all you have to do is step inside a  different universe and you can do  whatever you want in that universe  because it won't affect  the main mcu however you can bring  things from other universes into our  main universe and then they do  affect our universe so just like toby  maguire spider-man  and andrew garfield spider-man can be  taken from their respective universes  and come into ours and help tom hall and  spider-man fight the sinister six  this can happen with mutants as well  right now it's been reported and rumored  by a few trades that ghostwriter is  actually going to be introduced in  doctor strange 2.  